setValue ( $key,  $subkey,  $entry,  $value,  $type)[private]

Sets a value in the registry. Now uses Win32Native COM methods instead of VBScript.





Parameters










string$key

The root key (e.g., HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE). 




string$subkey

The subkey path. 




string$entry

The entry name. 




string | null$value

The value to set (optional). 




string$type

The type of value to set (e.g., SetStringValue). 







                Returns


bool True if the value was set successfully, false otherwise. 




